From 2ac8d524e79c7be6fb34c8f6470b1691c07e23ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flip-engineer <will.a.hargis@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:07:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/19] Re-enter the wake gate from the post-reset continuation
 (#797, #823)

The continuation dispatched --dispatch-message, which delivers directly and never evaluates the usage gate, so a capped or stale segment could deliver owed input before the reset. It now runs --wake-message, routed to Wake.message_cli -> drive_id -> Receive.wake_due, so the gate is re-read when it fires: a still-held window reports and reschedules, an elapsed one admits, and a handled message is a no-op. The fixture exercises the wake entry with a held check, elapsed delivery once, handled no-op, duplicate continuations, and a far reset that never delivers.

(cherry picked from commit 954c86da770dbacd3462daee49bf8759d1352bf7)
